-<div class="insight"><strong>Finding:</strong> Two clean behavioral regimes. DeepSeek and OpenAI are uniformly <strong style="color:var(--ac)">EXPLORATORY</strong> — 100% correctness, ~all constraints met, high novelty (0.82–0.91), and basin escape of 0.68–0.78: they leave the seed and find new solutions. Claude is <strong style="color:var(--am)">MIXED</strong> — conservative, exploratory, or wasteful depending on the story — with lower escape (0.44–0.48) and novelty (0.52–0.59), but ~3× higher code quality (0.13–0.17 vs 0.04–0.09) and the cleanest LSP output. The Claude correctness gap (0.55–0.58) is the subscription CLI's session-timeout limit, not a capability gap. And the <strong style="color:var(--cy)">EFFICIENT</strong> archetype is empty — no model is simultaneously cheap, reliable, clean, and basin-stable.</div>
