-<div class="insight" style="border-left-color:var(--success)"><strong style="color:var(--success)">Cleanliness is decoupled from cost too:</strong> the cheapest model (Flash) has the most LSP errors (13.5/story) and the lowest code-quality score (0.035), while the next-cheapest (Luna) has the cleanest LSP (5.1). Claude Haiku ($1.59) scores 0.167 on code quality — ~5× Flash's. Paying more buys neither fewer diagnostics nor higher cleanliness; these signals move independently of price.</div>
